---
layout: base
---

<article>
  {% set postNumber = collections.publicWeeknotes | getPostNumber(page) %}
  {% set postVersion = page.inputPath | postVersion %}
  {# Publish date from git history, like the colophon; front-matter date is
     the fallback for drafts and uncommitted files. Set before the
     supergraphic, which shows the same date in its own format. #}
  {% set headerDate = date %}
  {% if postVersion and postVersion.published %}
    {% set headerDate = postVersion.published %}
  {% endif %}
  {#- Supergraphic: the post's own facts set huge, set against the column's
     left edge. Four lines — the week number, the date, the version and the
     weight.

     It briefly carried the whole colophon. Everything cut since has been cut
     for the same reason, so the order is worth keeping straight: the two
     timestamps went first, being the two longest lines by half again and the
     only two that ever overhung the screen, and the word count and the colour
     followed. Read at this size they were a hex string and a bare number with
     nothing to say what either was — a colophon's values without a colophon's
     labels. What stayed is what a reader can place unaided.

     Every line is tabular figures or fixed text, which is what lets
     supergraphic.css size the whole graphic from one measured advance width.
     The colophon at the foot of the post still carries all six values with
     their labels, and is the record.

     Accessibility: the first two lines stay in the tree, because the
     supergraphic is the only place the week number appears at all and it
     reads before the title, which is the order it would have had. The
     colophon values do not — they are already on this page as real text with
     labels, and read here they would be bare numbers between the week note
     and the title. So the graphic says what it alone can say and the colophon
     says the rest.

     Not selectable either way: what a sighted reader sees is cropped type,
     and a selection over it would be nonsense.

     Only week notes have a number, and without one there is nothing to set. -#}
  {% if postNumber %}
  <p class="supergraphic">
    {#- Zero-padded, which with tabular figures makes this line measure the
       same on every post — and it is now the longest line in the stack, so it
       is the one that decides whether anything overhangs the screen at all. -#}
    <span>Week note {% if postNumber < 10 %}0{% endif %}{{ postNumber }}</span>
    <span>{{ headerDate | dateNumeric }}</span>
    {%- if postVersion %}
    <span aria-hidden="true">
      <span>{{ postVersion.version }}{% if postVersion.draft %} (draft){% endif %}</span>
      {#- Substituted after the build by src/_11ty/page-weight.js, the same
         token the colophon carries — it replaces every occurrence, and the
         fixed point it solves for counts both. -#}
      <span>@@PAGE_WEIGHT_KB@@ kB</span>
    </span>
    {%- endif %}
  </p>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="post-header">
    <h1 class="page-title">{{ title }}</h1>
    {% if description %}
      <p class="post-description">{{ description }}</p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  <hr>
  <div class="post-content">
    {{ content | safe }}
  </div>
  <hr>
  {% if postVersion %}
    <div class="post-colophon">
      <h2 class="post-colophon-label">Colophon</h2>
      <dl class="colophon-list">
      <dt>Version</dt>
      <dd>{{ postVersion.version }}{% if postVersion.draft %} (draft){% endif %}</dd>
      {% if postVersion.published %}
        <dt>Published</dt>
        <dd><time datetime="{{ postVersion.published | isoDate }}">{{ postVersion.published | dateTimeFormat }}</time></dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if postVersion.updated %}
        <dt>Last updated</dt>
        <dd><time datetime="{{ postVersion.updated | isoDate }}">{{ postVersion.updated | dateTimeFormat }}</time></dd>
      {% endif %}
      {#- Substituted after the build by src/_11ty/page-weight.js, which can
         only weigh this document once it has been written. -#}
      <dt>Weight</dt>
      <dd>@@PAGE_WEIGHT_KB@@ kB</dd>
      <dt>Words</dt>
      <dd>{{ content | wordCount }}</dd>
      <dt>Colour</dt>
      <dd>{{ page.fileSlug | postColor }}</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</article>
